Thought: To evaluate the XGBoost model, I need to perform two main tasks: evaluate the model on the test set and perform cross-validation. First, I will list the files in the directory to locate the test data and any other necessary files.
Action: list_files
Action Input: {"path": "/Users/n0w0f/chained_ml_gpt_react_nitride/prepare_ml_ready_dataset_trial_0/nitride_ml_dataset", "recursive": true}

Thought: I have located the test data file (`test.csv`) and the training data file (`train.csv`). Now, I will evaluate the XGBoost model using the test data to obtain the test set evaluation metrics.
Action: evaluate_xgboost_model
Action Input: {"model_path": "/Users/n0w0f/chained_ml_gpt_react_nitride/train_xgboost_formation_energy_model_trial_0/trained_xgboost_model.pkl", "test_data_path": "/Users/n0w0f/chained_ml_gpt_react_nitride/prepare_ml_ready_dataset_trial_0/nitride_ml_dataset/test.csv", "target_column": "formation_energy_per_atom", "detailed_analysis": true}

Thought: I have obtained the test set evaluation metrics, including `mae`, `rmse`, `r2`, and `feature_importance`. Next, I will perform cross-validation on the training data to obtain the cross-validation results.
Action: perform_cross_validation
Action Input: {"train_data_path": "/Users/n0w0f/chained_ml_gpt_react_nitride/prepare_ml_ready_dataset_trial_0/nitride_ml_dataset/train.csv", "target_column": "formation_energy_per_atom", "cv_folds": 5}

